  "status": "approved",
  "title": "",
  "classification": {
    "primarySkillId": "lcm-two-numbers",
    "secondarySkillIds": [
      "hcf-two-numbers",
      "prime-factorisation"
    ],
    "reasoningScore": 30,
    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "Apply the demonstrated prime-factorisation method to six pairs of whole numbers and check with a calculator."
  },
  "content": {
    "id": "p72-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Write each pair of numbers as their prime factors and hence determine the HCF and LCM.\nCheck your answer using a calculator.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p72-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "315 and 90",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$315=3^{2}\\cdot5\\cdot7$, $90=2\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot5$.\nHCF: $45$; LCM: $630$.",
          "worked": "Align the prime bases, including zero powers for absent primes.\n$$\\begin{align*}315&=2^{0}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot5^{1}\\cdot7^{1}\\\\90&=2^{1}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot5^{1}\\cdot7^{0}\\end{align*}$$\nUse the smallest powers for the HCF and the largest powers for the LCM.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{HCF}(315,90)&=2^{0}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot5^{1}\\cdot7^{0}\\\\\\operatorname{HCF}(315,90)&=45\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(315,90)&=2^{1}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot5^{1}\\cdot7^{1}\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(315,90)&=630\\end{align*}$$\nCalculator check: $\\operatorname{GCD}(315,90)=45$ and $\\operatorname{LCM}(315,90)=630$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      },
      {
        "id": "p72-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "180 and 252",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$180=2^{2}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot5$, $252=2^{2}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot7$.\nHCF: $36$; LCM: $1260$.",
          "worked": "Align the prime bases, including zero powers for absent primes.\n$$\\begin{align*}180&=2^{2}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot5^{1}\\cdot7^{0}\\\\252&=2^{2}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot5^{0}\\cdot7^{1}\\end{align*}$$\nUse the smallest powers for the HCF and the largest powers for the LCM.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{HCF}(180,252)&=2^{2}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot5^{0}\\cdot7^{0}\\\\\\operatorname{HCF}(180,252)&=36\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(180,252)&=2^{2}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot5^{1}\\cdot7^{1}\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(180,252)&=1260\\end{align*}$$\nCalculator check: $\\operatorname{GCD}(180,252)=36$ and $\\operatorname{LCM}(180,252)=1260$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 72
      },
      {
        "id": "p72-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "900 and 1620",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$900=2^{2}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot5^{2}$, $1620=2^{2}\\cdot3^{4}\\cdot5$.\nHCF: $180$; LCM: $8100$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}900&=2^{2}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot5^{2}\\\\1620&=2^{2}\\cdot3^{4}\\cdot5^{1}\\end{align*}$$\nUse the smallest powers for the HCF and the largest powers for the LCM.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{HCF}(900,1620)&=2^{2}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot5^{1}\\\\\\operatorname{HCF}(900,1620)&=180\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(900,1620)&=2^{2}\\cdot3^{4}\\cdot5^{2}\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(900,1620)&=8100\\end{align*}$$\nCalculator check: $\\operatorname{GCD}(900,1620)=180$ and $\\operatorname{LCM}(900,1620)=8100$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      },
      {
        "id": "p72-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "756 and 1008",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$756=2^{2}\\cdot3^{3}\\cdot7$, $1008=2^{4}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot7$.\nHCF: $252$; LCM: $3024$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}756&=2^{2}\\cdot3^{3}\\cdot7^{1}\\\\1008&=2^{4}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot7^{1}\\end{align*}$$\nUse the smallest powers for the HCF and the largest powers for the LCM.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{HCF}(756,1008)&=2^{2}\\cdot3^{2}\\cdot7^{1}\\\\\\operatorname{HCF}(756,1008)&=252\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(756,1008)&=2^{4}\\cdot3^{3}\\cdot7^{1}\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(756,1008)&=3024\\end{align*}$$\nCalculator check: $\\operatorname{GCD}(756,1008)=252$ and $\\operatorname{LCM}(756,1008)=3024$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p72-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "1152 and 1728",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1152=2^{7}\\cdot3^{2}$, $1728=2^{6}\\cdot3^{3}$.\nHCF: $576$; LCM: $3456$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}1152&=2^{7}\\cdot3^{2}\\\\1728&=2^{6}\\cdot3^{3}\\end{align*}$$\nUse the smallest powers for the HCF and the largest powers for the LCM.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{HCF}(1152,1728)&=2^{6}\\cdot3^{2}\\\\\\operatorname{HCF}(1152,1728)&=576\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(1152,1728)&=2^{7}\\cdot3^{3}\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(1152,1728)&=3456\\end{align*}$$\nCalculator check: $\\operatorname{GCD}(1152,1728)=576$ and $\\operatorname{LCM}(1152,1728)=3456$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 66
      },
      {
        "id": "p72-q1-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "2450 and 3675",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2450=2\\cdot5^{2}\\cdot7^{2}$, $3675=3\\cdot5^{2}\\cdot7^{2}$.\nHCF: $1225$; LCM: $7350$.",
          "worked": "Align the prime bases, including zero powers for absent primes.\n$$\\begin{align*}2450&=2^{1}\\cdot3^{0}\\cdot5^{2}\\cdot7^{2}\\\\3675&=2^{0}\\cdot3^{1}\\cdot5^{2}\\cdot7^{2}\\end{align*}$$\nUse the smallest powers for the HCF and the largest powers for the LCM.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{HCF}(2450,3675)&=2^{0}\\cdot3^{0}\\cdot5^{2}\\cdot7^{2}\\\\\\operatorname{HCF}(2450,3675)&=1225\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(2450,3675)&=2^{1}\\cdot3^{1}\\cdot5^{2}\\cdot7^{2}\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(2450,3675)&=7350\\end{align*}$$\nCalculator check: $\\operatorname{GCD}(2450,3675)=1225$ and $\\operatorname{LCM}(2450,3675)=7350$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
      }
    ]
  },
